  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building High Judicial Institute</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen the institutional capacity of the High Judicial Institute (HJI) of Libya, which is the training institute for the justice sector, in order to enhance its ability to train the judiciary and drafters of laws in relatively new but increasingly important legal fields such as financial crime, organized crime and human trafficking. The capacity of graduates from the institute &#x2013; who become staff of the Prosecutor&#x2019;s Office, public lawyers, government lawyers (and in a later state potentially judges) and law drafters &#x2013; and of participants in on-the-job-trainings is improved to better deal with cases in these fields.Ultimately the project aims to improve effectiveness, efficiency, organisational, analytical and policy making capacities. By improving the role and function of the HJI, the institution can strengthen the further development of the Rule of Law and Good Governance in Libya and therewith improve the confidence of the Libyan people in the justice sector.The project also aims at fostering and improving the bilateral relations between the Netherlands and Libya.</narrative>
  </description>
